WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.940
<b>Buzou Prefectural High School</b>

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.740
<b>Quiz Bowl Circle 
New Students Welcome!! 
100-Question Paper Quiz</b>

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.390
The quiz bowl circle?

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.630
Do you study quizzes?

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:22.910
You're just a circle?

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.570
Question.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.290
What is quiz bowl?

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.010
<b>Quiz Bowl Circle 
New Students Welcome!! 
100-Question Paper Quiz</b>

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:37.300
Quiz bowl is a game known by 
everyone around the world.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.760
There are those who take it quite seriously!

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.730
Now follow in the footsteps of the pioneers 
who upheld the quiz bowl craze long ago!

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.810
You, too!

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.270
Don't you want to become a quiz king?!

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.700
Huh?!

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:17.340
<b>Fastest Finger First</b>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.250
<b>Question 1: "Don't You Want to Become a Quiz King?"</b>

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.250
<i>Quiz king? What is that?</i>

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.080
<i>And who is this huge guy?</i>

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.710
Give this a try.

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.340
You try it, too.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.340
And you two.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.550
Here. Try this.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.320
Sasajima! Back off!

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.330
Circles don't belong here!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.080
New students, join the baseball team!

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.910
<i>It's my second day of high school.</i>

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.770
<i>And today is the day the battle between
the school clubs for new students begins.</i>

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:54.720
<i>This is a world that I, 
Koshiyama Shiki, don't belong in...</i>

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.970
Quiz, huh?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.970
Kuroda? From the Nishi 
Middle basketball team?

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:14.380
Still playing in high school, too?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:16.050
You better believe it!

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.760
My first goal is to take nationals!

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.620
Take your seats.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:26.100
So what did you all think about 
yesterday's entrance ceremony?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.600
Three years of high school may 
seem long now, but it'll fly by.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.370
You can focus solely on your studies,

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.360
or you can work hard at your clubs.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:38.600
<i>If I had a large physique 
or some kind of skill,</i>

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.860
<i>would I have worked hard at some club, too?</i>

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.280
<b>Quiz Bowl Circle 
New Students Welcome!! 
100-Question Paper Quiz</b>

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.780
<i>A paper quiz?</i>

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.820
<i>What in the world? 
They're all quiz questions?</i>

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:57.500
<i>So people who like quizzes get together and 
spend their time answering quiz questions?</i>

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.010
<i>Is that supposed to be fun?</i>

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.420
Don't you want to become a quiz king?

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.100
<i>And that guy was part of it?</i>

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.680
<i>I'm not sure I want to...</i>

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:10.060
We'll spend first period choosing 
your class representatives.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.560
Let's start with the class officers...

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:13.210
<i>Question 1.</i>

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:17.620
<i>Japan's Three Non-Nuclear Principles are "to 
neither possess, manufacture, nor..." what?</i>

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.000
<i>"Introduce." That's common sense.</i>

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.030
<i>Question 2... Let's see...</i>

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.880
<i>"I think, therefore I am" is a quote by... 
Descartes, of course.</i>

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.530
<i>What desert in Africa is the 
largest hot desert in the world?</i>

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.500
<i>Even elementary school kids know that.</i>

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:36.580
Introduce 
René Descartes 
Sahara Desert

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:40.140
<i>"As Gregor Samsa awoke one 
morning out of restless dreams"</i>

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:43.940
<i>is the opening line of which 
novel by Franz Kafka?</i>

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:47.170
<i>Well, I guess some of these are 
fairly specialized questions,</i>

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:50.600
<i>but if even I know the answers, 
this must be pretty low-level...</i>

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.900
Next up, librarians. 
We'll need one boy and one girl.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.410
Any volunteers?

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:02.030
Here... Here... Here, here... Here...

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.400
Sure, I'll do it.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.490
All right, Inoue Daisuke. It's all yours.

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:12.750
<i>But I was the class librarian through 
all three years of middle school!</i>

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.640
Did you see that?

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.210
I guess he wanted to do it.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.300
Now, how about a girl?

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:22.730
Me.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:24.720
A volunteer?

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.550
Yes. I'm Fukami Mari.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:31.010
<i>Does she like books, too?</i>

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.390
Fukami-san's really pretty, huh?

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.970
Looks like you got some side perks.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.140
Man, quit teasing me!

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.680
<i>Whoops, that was close.</i>

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.400
<i>If I'd gotten the same 
job as the popular girl,</i>

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.650
<i>I'd never hear the end of it.</i>

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.790
<i>Our eyes met!</i>

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:51.410
<i>Oh...</i>

00:05:52.730 --> 00:05:56.040
<i>I ended up answering all the quiz questions.</i>

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.880
<i>This might not be a bad way to kill time.</i>

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:02.800
<i>No, no, no, no! No way!</i>

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.260
Let's hit the school shop.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.050
I'll push our desks together.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:09.430
Seriously?

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.220
He should just speak up.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:15.190
Isn't he lonely?

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:16.180
Don't!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.890
<b>Library</b>

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.460
<i>They have a lot of minor series, too.</i>

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.760
<i>There are so many more genres than 
the middle school library had!</i>

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:48.730
<i>The library is where I got my start.</i>

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:53.250
<i>Ever since elementary school, I've spent 
more time reading than playing with friends.</i>

00:06:54.670 --> 00:07:00.220
<i>I didn't want to play with the kids who 
called me "shrimp" and  "dunce," anyway.</i>

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:03.900
<i>It was just the only way I 
knew to have fun on my own.</i>

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.110
<b>Buzou Prefectural Library</b>

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:07.440
<i>Since my mom worked at
the library, I spent every day</i>

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.860
<i>there reading until she got off work.</i>

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.580
<i>In middle school, I became 
the class librarian.</i>

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:16.610
<i>By then, I was nothing but a bookworm.</i>

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:21.340
<i>I used to read a lot of classical literature and non-fictional works back then...</i>

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.280
<i>It stimulated my imagination and 
opened up new worlds before me.</i>

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:32.100
<i>But I was never able to find any friends 
to share the joy of reading with.</i>

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.570
<i>I thought that was fine, though.</i>

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:40.060
<i>Of course, it meant I had no 
connection to any girls, either...</i>

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.660
Let's see...

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:52.660
<i>Isn't she the class librarian, Fukami-san?</i>

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.790
<i>Wait, does she even see me?!</i>

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:01.500
U-Um, watch—

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.290
Huh?

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.080
A-Are you o—

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:10.760
Oh!

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:13.220
<i>P-P-Pan—</i>

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:14.690
Everything okay?

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:16.680
I-I just tripped! That's all!

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.190
No running!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.370
You can't eat your lunch here!

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:27.800
I'm sorry!

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.560
<i>Man, that startled me...</i>

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.210
<i>Forget about that!</i>

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:35.110
<i>My safe haven will be tainted
 with this crazy memory!</i>

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.540
Is this Fukami-san's?

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.840
<i>What are these marks?</i>

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.370
<b>...long house / is known as...</b>

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.380
<b>...refer to betting money / on a single...</b>

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.380
<b>...marks left / behind in the snow...</b>

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.340
And finally,

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:55.470
the best perk of being in 
the hardball tennis club

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:59.100
is that you get to see sights like this 
at the girls' court next to ours!

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:57.890
There!

00:08:58.150 --> 00:08:59.100
There!

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:00.510
<i>So wrong...</i>

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.560
And that concludes the introduction
 of all the school clubs.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:06.940
<i>Me getting in to a sports club is a joke,</i>

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.520
<i>but I'm not that interested 
in the culture clubs, either.</i>

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:15.780
<b>Welcome, New Students!</b>

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:13.340
Next, we'll introduce the 
school associations.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:15.780
Here's the quiz bowl circle. Go ahead.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.740
<i>Oh, the quiz king...</i>

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.510
Ah. Test, test.

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:24.200
I'm the president of the quiz bowl 
circle, Sasajima Gakuto, second-year.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:31.160
Who wants to go to New York?!

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:37.450
There was once a quiz show by that 
name on TV. Do you remember it?

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:41.180
It was, indeed, a world in which 
people competed in quiz bowl.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:46.500
Even today, there is a major quiz 
show called <i>High School Quiz</i>,

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:51.330
in which high school students engage 
in a heated competition every year.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:54.360
Any high school student may participate.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.260
Quiz bowl, as everyone knows,

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:02.480
is a game anyone can play where
one simply answers questions to win.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:06.330
However, adding a competitive 
aspect makes it a sport.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:09.040
<i>A sport? Quiz bowl?</i>

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:12.000
The first step is to experience quiz bowl.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:14.960
Hence this impromptu quiz meet!

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:18.180
The first six to raise their 
hands will get to participate!

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.510
The true thrill of quiz bowl is 
competing to buzz in the fastest!

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:24.890
Nothing can match the rush that 
comes from pressing this buzzer!

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:27.850
<i>Where do they even sell those things?</i>

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:30.140
Me, me! I wanna do it!

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:31.230
Yeah, me too!

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:32.700
Here.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.820
<i>Fukami Mari?</i>

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.060
Please come up to the stage.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:39.450
R-Right.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:43.850
<i>She looks so meek,</i>

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:45.430
<i>but she's so assertive!</i>

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.070
<i>I could never do that.</i>

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.720
In the interest of time,

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:54.380
I'll select the remaining three 
participants at random.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.580
Class A, female, student number 6.

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.080
What?!

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:59.440
Class C, female, number 8.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.750
You're kidding! No way!

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:01.120
Class D, male, number 11.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.720
Koshiyama, isn't that you?

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:08.900
Class D, male, student number 11.
 I'm number 10.

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:09.780
Huh?

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.980
<i>What?! I have to go up there?!</i>

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.540
<i>With all these people watching?!</i>

00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:18.020
<i>I can't! I can't! I can't! I can't!</i>

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:19.580
<i>This isn't even funny!</i>

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.990
<b>Flail</b>

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.990
<b>Flail</b>

00:11:24.630 --> 00:11:26.740
<i>How did this happen?</i>

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.610
<i>And the mood up here is so awkward...</i>

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:34.960
Question.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:42.970
"Avril" in French, "aprile" in Italian, and 
"April" in English refer to which month?

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:44.970
<i>April?</i>

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:47.430
April!

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.310
Correct, but that was terrible!

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.310
Huh?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.930
You didn't do it right at all.

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:53.690
You weren't taking it the 
least bit seriously.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:55.940
You could have buzzed in much faster!

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.900
Uh... Well...

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:00.960
The key to being the fastest finger 
is just what it sounds like:

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:03.050
to move your finger the fastest!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.530
If you don't earn the right to respond, 
you can't give the right answer!

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:08.740
<i>I get what he's saying, but...</i>

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:09.990
Question.

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:13.250
There are stars on the American flag—

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.200
<i>That was fast! Someone pushed it already?</i>

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:16.710
The Stars and Stripes.

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:18.150
Huh?!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:21.150
There's more to the question.

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:27.980
There are stars on the American flag, 
one for each state. How many are there?

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.720
The correct answer is 50.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.550
A trick question?

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:35.440
Some questions are very straightforward,

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.190
but others can't be answered until 
you hear the complete question.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:39.480
You must be careful.

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:43.700
<i>See? You have to listen until 
the end before you can answer.</i>

00:12:44.420 --> 00:12:47.910
From this point on, try using 
your imaginations more.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:51.060
<i>As in try to predict the 
last part of the question?</i>

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.330
Here's the question.

00:12:53.330 --> 00:12:57.470
The nation with the largest 
land area is Russia,

00:12:57.470 --> 00:12:58.090
and the nation—

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:03.260
<i>The nation... with the 
second largest land area?</i>

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.680
<i>Second is Canada, and third is America...</i>

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:09.220
...with the smallest land area is which?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.310
<i>Vatican City!</i>

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.820
Vatican City!

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:13.870
Correct.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:14.850
Yes!

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:17.310
<i>So it was the opposite of the largest!</i>

00:13:18.510 --> 00:13:20.500
<i>I know the answers, but...</i>

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.100
Are you new to fast buzzing?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.500
Uh... It's my first time.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:33.500
If you buzz after you know the 
answer, you'll be too late.

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:37.500
Fast buzzing can determine the winner 
by a margin of 0.01 seconds.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.950
R-Right...

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.960
There's no time to waste 
on thinking things over.

00:13:43.410 --> 00:13:45.880
<i>Wh-What is she talking about?</i>

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:49.510
<i>She volunteered for this, but she 
hasn't pressed the buzzer once!</i>

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.890
<i>N-No, her panties have 
nothing to do with this!</i>

00:13:58.580 --> 00:13:59.610
<i>Her face changed...</i>

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:00.850
Question.

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:02.820
French for "flash of lightni—"

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:10.280
Please give your answer.

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:13.240
Éclair.

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:14.820
Correct.

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:18.970
Question.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:21.590
"Et tu, Brute—"

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:22.920
<i>Julius Caesar</i>.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:24.320
Correct.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:25.770
<i>Wait...</i>

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:26.860
Question.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:27.800
"Jumping flea—"

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:29.480
Ukulele.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:30.410
Correct.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:35.590
<i>Wait a minute... How does she know 
what the question's going to be?</i>

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:42.470
What? I'm not cheating, okay?

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.850
I-I wasn't...

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:50.000
There's a point in questions you can answer 
early where the answer becomes certain.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.280
Of course, these have all 
been really basic questions.

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:56.000
Points? Basic?

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:57.590
Question.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.210
The three great festivals of Kyoto—

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.620
<i>Whoa, that was fast!</i>

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.210
<i>Wait, it wasn't Fukami-san!</i>

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:03.980
Yes! I got it!

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:05.660
Please give your answer.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:06.170
Oh...

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:07.600
Um...

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.790
The time limit is five seconds.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.300
No, that—

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.140
An interesting answer, but incorrect.

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:16.860
<i>That rattled me.</i>

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:20.680
I will read the question one more time.

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.060
The three great festivals of Kyoto are...

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:25.320
<i>The three great festivals of Kyoto are</i>

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.780
<i>the Gion Festival, the Festival of 
Ages, and the Hollyhock Festival.</i>

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:30.460
...May's Hollyhock Festival, Jul—

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:33.520
<i>"Jul"? That'll be July, the Gion Festival!</i>

00:15:33.520 --> 00:15:35.160
<i>So the only answer remaining is...</i>

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.940
The Festival of Ages.

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:37.850
Correct.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:40.540
<b>..."to neither possess, ma/nufacture, nor..." what?</b>

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:41.540
<i>So that's it...</i>

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.580
<b>...orange, gr/een, and...</b>

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.150
<i>I'm starting to get it now!</i>

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:42.580
<b>...melody, rhy/thm...</b>

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:43.920
<b>..."to neither possess, ma/nufacture, nor..." what?
...three elements of music are melody, rhy/thm, and...
...orange, gr/een, and what?
...cannot move are the bi/shop and what?</b>

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:47.350
<i>What should I do? Should I try to buzz in?</i>

00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:48.760
<i>I want to try answering!</i>

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:51.430
Now, let's try some harder questions.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:52.770
<i>Harder?</i>

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:55.730
<i>What's important is to 
earn the right to answer.</i>

00:15:56.740 --> 00:16:00.230
Fast buzzing can determine the winner 
by a margin of 0.01 seconds.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:03.480
There's a point in questions you can answer 
early where the answer becomes certain.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:05.920
<i>If I can predict the question,</i>

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.900
<i>I'll have five seconds 
to answer after buzzing.</i>

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.950
<i>There should be time to think about it then.</i>

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:13.080
Question.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:17.540
"I fell in love. This was something new."

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.750
<i>I did it! I buzzed!</i>

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:24.250
<i>Wait, he knows this one? Was it intuition?</i>

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:26.720
Please give your answer.

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.720
<i>I know this! It's the opening 
line of that novel!</i>

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:34.220
<b>...by which French author?</b>

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:36.090
<i>There were other literature questions
 like this on that paper quiz, too!</i>

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:36.680
<b>...which novel by Franz Kafka?</b>

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.010
<b>...which female Heian Period author?</b>

00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.440
<i>If this question is also looking 
for the title or author,</i>

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:41.180
<i>which is it?</i>

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:42.640
Three seconds.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:45.000
<i>If this is really a "hard" question...</i>

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:47.560
Two.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:50.150
The answer is...

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:50.610
eniemeG saD

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:01.540
Correct!

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.130
This is the opening line of which 
literary work by Dazai Osamu?

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:09.850
The answer is 

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:12.050
I'm impressed you knew such 
a lesser-known title!

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:15.170
<i>Everyone's really looking at me now...</i>

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:18.440
Sasajima, you're running over!

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:22.030
Just when it was getting good...

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:24.140
You! What's your name and class?

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:27.800
Uh... Class D, K-Koshiyama.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:32.320
Then let's give a hand to Koshiyama-kun 
for answering the last question!

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:45.540
In quiz bowl, your age, sex, 
and physique are irrelevant.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.250
The more you participate, the more 
knowledge and experience you gain.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:52.030
That's true for everyone!

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:55.420
That's right! Anyone can 
take part in quiz bowl!

00:17:57.460 --> 00:17:58.810
<i>Nailed it.</i>

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:03.100
And that was the quiz bowl 
circle's introduction.

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:08.060
They say quiz bowl is popular 
in theological schools lately.

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:09.750
Come to think of it, that boy,

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.860
Sasajima-kun, transferred here last year.

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:15.320
From Kaijou High School, I believe.

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:23.560
<i>Oh, man... My heart is still racing.</i>

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:26.740
<i>I can't believe I did something 
so new in front of that crowd.</i>

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:28.460
<i>But...</i>

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:32.170
<i>The moment I pressed that 
buzzer felt really good.</i>

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.890
Quiz buzzers are surprisingly easy to break,

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:38.550
so try not to press them too hard.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:44.260
Um, when I tripped in the library...

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.480
I-I'm sorry! That was—

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:51.610
Did I drop that paper 
with the quiz questions?

00:18:51.970 --> 00:18:52.940
Huh? Oh...

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:56.080
Th-That's right. I forgot.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:56.780
Here.

00:19:01.190 --> 00:19:04.030
Did you look up these answers somewhere?

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:06.750
Oh, wrong one!

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:09.460
Here's yours! That one's mine!

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:11.840
Thanks.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:13.930
You know...

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:19.080
I didn't understand what those 
little marks were at first.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:19.630
But...

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:23.120
Are they to mark the points 
you talked about earlier?

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.260
Where the answer to the question is certain?

00:19:26.030 --> 00:19:27.060
Huh?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:29.520
S-Sorry if I'm wrong.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:35.110
You... really are smart, aren't you?

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:38.100
No, I don't think...

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.430
When you answered the last question,

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:43.540
how did you know the title 
would be the right answer?

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:47.440
Oh, because the president said 
it'd be a hard question.

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:52.520
Rather than its famous author, the title 
of a minor work is more... well...

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.130
I figured that would be harder to answer.

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:58.410
Did you say that was your first quiz match?

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:00.590
Yeah, of the fast buzzing kind.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:04.800
Y-You're forgiven for seeing my panties!

00:20:04.800 --> 00:20:06.680
<i>Where'd that come from?!</i>

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:07.770
But in return...

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:11.230
Join the quiz circle with me!

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:14.940
<i>Wh-Wh-What is she saying?!</i>

00:20:15.490 --> 00:20:18.600
It was your first quiz match, 
but in such a short time,

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:21.470
you managed to get the hang of quiz bowl.

00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:23.790
And the knowledge you have...

00:20:24.190 --> 00:20:29.510
Even if I'd heard that last question 
to the end, I couldn't have buzzed.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:32.040
I didn't know the answer!

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:36.010
<i>What? I didn't just beat her to the buzzer?</i>

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:38.790
Same with this paper quiz.

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:41.650
There were several questions 
I didn't know the answers to,

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:44.580
but you answered almost all of them!

00:20:44.580 --> 00:20:47.710
Your abundant knowledge and quick thinking

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.630
will be amazing weapons!

00:20:50.360 --> 00:20:53.140
I believe you can become the quiz king!

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:55.960
<i>The quiz king...</i>

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:32.860
Everyone, welcome to the world of quiz bowl!

00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:36.770
I am the quiz master, here to share 
the fun of quiz bowl with all of you!

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:39.000
Koshiyama-kun, congratulations 
on your quiz debut!

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.710
Th-Thank you.

00:22:40.950 --> 00:22:45.260
This may surprise you, but "7O3X" 
is also a quiz bowl term.

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:47.090
Fukami-kun, do you know what it means?

00:22:47.320 --> 00:22:49.440
Yes! Get seven right and you win,

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:49.090
<b>7 Correct Answers</b>

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:51.100
<b>3 Incorrect Answers</b>

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:51.010
but get three wrong and you fail.

00:22:51.010 --> 00:22:53.350
It's a basic rule of quiz bowl!

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:56.300
That's right! The path to victory is steep!

00:22:56.300 --> 00:22:58.250
Start heading there today, 
one step at a time!

00:22:58.250 --> 00:22:59.490
We'll do our best!
